Z||000000||jaguiler||10-15-2001||11:22 PM||||Hello all!<P>It has been a while since I posted.  Tongiht I was looking for an old post I saw a long time ago, I just can't find it, so I will ask the question, maybe someone will recognise it.<P>I notice that my 86 GT vibrates at speeds above 70+ mph.  The vibration seems to start in the back of the car and work it's way forward, under my seat, then to the front of the car... I can hear the vibrationin the doors, mirrors, feel it on my seat.<BR>The pattern is always the same, the vibration starts in the back and works its way to the front of the car.<P>Any ideas?  I just got a house with a garage, so I may be changing my bushing, I work by yself, any suggestions?<P>John<P>------------------<BR><BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||64.157.190.156||reg||6
Z||000001||gomobile||10-16-2001||10:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jaguiler:<BR><B>Hello all!<P>It has been a while since I posted.  Tongiht I was looking for an old post I saw a long time ago, I just can't find it, so I will ask the question, maybe someone will recognise it.<P>I notice that my 86 GT vibrates at speeds above 70+ mph.  The vibration seems to start in the back of the car and work it's way forward, under my seat, then to the front of the car... I can hear the vibrationin the doors, mirrors, feel it on my seat.<BR>The pattern is always the same, the vibration starts in the back and works its way to the front of the car.<P>Any ideas?  I just got a house with a garage, so I may be changing my bushing, I work by yself, any suggestions?<P>John<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My 1st suspect is the infamous DOG_BONE (very important especially since you say that vibrartion comes from back)<P>PS: I say this cause I had a similiar problem - I ended changing the dog_bone since the other one was worn out already. Now<BR>I only get a slight virbration at the front but then again it would not be a FIERO (grin). Though I do need some better tires.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000002||jaguiler||10-16-2001||10:58 AM||||How can I tell if it is the dogbone,  I did a visual inspection and it looks ok.  I imagine changing those bushings must be pretty easy.<P>- recap -  my vibration "moves" or migrates from the back to the front, in cycles.... about once every 8-10 seconds....<BR>any ideas anyone?<P>------------------<BR><BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||209.246.221.183||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||10-16-2001||11:12 AM||||If the dogbone is "bad" you should be able to rock the engine by hand.  There should be very little movement with the engine if the dog bone bushings are good.<P>As for vibrations, I suggest tire balance.  I had all four tires rebalanced this summer and all the vibrations I felt vanished. ||||reg||1
